  "result": "I fixed the duplicate deliveries in `src/lib/event-bus.ts`. I haven't run the test suite or a detach/re-attach cycle to check it.\n\n**Cause:** `subscribe` copies the handler set each time, but the function it returned deleted from the set it had captured when it ran. Any later subscribe to the same event type replaced that set, so detaching removed the handler from an old copy and left it live. Each re-register then stacked another copy of the webhook, audit and usage handlers.\n\n**Fix:** the returned unsubscribe function now looks up the current set, copies it without that handler, and stores the copy. The copy-on-write behaviour during `emit()` is kept. Detaching a handler that is already gone does nothing.\n\nRegistering again without detaching first was already a no-op (the guard in `event-registry.ts`), and I left that alone. In-app notifications subscribe once at import and are never detached, so they stay delivered once, including while the other handlers are detached.",
